{
  "title": "Condition Caveats & Indentation",
  "subtitle": "Common Pitfalls & The Single vs Double Equals Trap",
  "topic": "4.1 • CAVEATS & RULES",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      4.1 • Syntax Pitfalls\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      <hlt>Indentation</hlt> & Pitfalls\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Python uses indentation (4 spaces) instead of curly brackets to know which code belongs inside the decision block.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fca5a5; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Trap 1 • Single = vs Double ==\n    </span>\n    <h3 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Assignment vs Equality Check</h3>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\n      Writing <code>if x = 10:</code> causes a <strong>SyntaxError</strong> because single <code>=</code> puts a value in a box. Always use <code>if x == 10:</code>!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 13px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># WRONG: if role = \"admin\": -> SyntaxError</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> role == <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"admin\"</span>:  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># CORRECT!</span><br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Access Granted\"</span>)\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #c4b5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Trap 2 • IndentationError\n    </span>\n    <h3 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">The 4-Space Rule</h3>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\n      Every line that belongs inside an <code>if</code> block must be indented by exactly 4 spaces (or 1 Tab).\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}